- **No distinct evidence exists for the hyphen folder:** there is no separate model, no separate weights, no separate harness run — only a differently-punctuated folder + an `opencode/` scaffold id.

> Provenance / conclusion: **one real artifact (Google Gemma 4 26B-A4B), two folders.** The canonical **dot** folder is scored (report 109); this **hyphen** stub is a duplicate whose only "content" is an 8-line spec meta with no benchmarks of its own. Scoring it would **double-count** the identical model and make my own two findings files count one artifact twice — prohibited by `RULES.md` and quarantined by `pnpm sync`. Note the curated queue itself lists **both** spellings (L116 `gemma-4.26b-a4b` @ 76 and L135 `gemma-4-26b-a4b` @ 72.6), confirming this is a dataset duplication rather than two models.
> Recommended curator resolution: **de-duplicate** — collapse `gemma-4-26b-a4b` (hyphen) into the canonical `gemma-4.26b-a4b` (dot, id `google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it`) and retire the stub folder, exactly as the sibling pair `gemma-4-12b-unified` (hyphen) / `gemma-4.12b-unified` (dot) should be merged. Until then this folder should carry **no separate score**; readers are pointed to [`../gemma-4.26b-a4b/`](../gemma-4.26b-a4b/).

